@Shawnsuun @DarkLight1337 following the request to consolidate #64934 here, I have opened the test-only contribution directly against this PR's branch: [Shawnsuun/vllm#1](https://github.com/Shawnsuun/vllm/pull/1).

It ports the existing signed-off mid-chat test from `9554969fb` as `417305b6e4938f6828a7daeb60a537c35fb459bd`: one file, 28 added lines, no implementation changes. It checks exact native `[user, system, user]` token parity for `[user, developer, user]`, two `[INST]` turns, and preservation of the caller's input.

Validation was rerun on **this branch's head `96cbb1e450` plus the test**: six renderer tests passed on CPU with the real cached Mistral tokenizer (`--noconftest`), and all applicable changed-file pre-commit hooks passed, including mypy and CI test tethering. Restoring the pre-fix renderer makes the added test fail with `ValueError: Unknown message role: developer`; restoring this implementation makes it pass. These results do not cover full repository fixtures, HTTP/GPU serving, or upstream CI.

@Shawnsuun could you review and merge or cherry-pick that test into this branch if it fits? After consolidation, @DarkLight1337 could you authorize upstream CI and the one-time automated review? The existing pre-run check is failed and pre-commit/CodeRabbit are skipped, so those validations remain outstanding. I support taking the implementation forward here rather than merging #64934 separately.

Thanks @juliendenize, confirmed. With mistral-common 1.13.1 and the renderer change reverted, both developer-role tests pass (`tests/renderers/test_mistral.py` + `tests/tokenizers_/test_mistral.py`: 72 passed, 2 skipped). On 1.13.0 they fail with `Unknown message role: developer`.

I pushed 20b54378fb, which:
- drops the renderer-side mapping, so `vllm/renderers/mistral.py` matches `main` again;
- raises the minimum to `mistral_common >= 1.13.1` in the same requirement files as #64169 (`pip-compile` hooks pass; 1.13.1 has the same dependencies as 1.13.0);
- keeps both regression tests, so the behaviour stays pinned.

I've updated the title and description to match.

